  "body": {
    "storage": {
      "value": "<ac:layout><ac:layout-section ac:type=\"two_right_sidebar\" ac:breakout-mode=\"default\"><ac:layout-cell><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"b54738aa-765b-499f-9f98-25833b8ac9ce\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>This feature is available from V0.93-Bahmni</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>Tests which cannot be performed locally can be referred out to external laboratories /centres and once the results are available, enter the same in the system.</p><h2>Used By</h2><p>It is used by lab technicians when executing lab orders and performing tests.</p><h2>How is it Used?</h2><h3>1. Refer tests to external laboratory / centre</h3><ol><li><p>Go to Samples Collected - Today tab, which will be listing all Lab orders of the patients for which the sample has been already collected today.</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"305\" ac:original-width=\"1078\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Lab Dashboard - Samples Collected.jpeg\" ri:version-at-save=\"2\" /></ac:image><p><strong>                                                               Lab Dashboard - Samples Collected</strong></p></li><li><p>Search the desired patient&rsquo;s order entering the Accession Number / Patient ID / Name in respective fields in the top row of the grid.</p></li><li><p>Click on the &ldquo;Result&rdquo; icon under the &ldquo;Action&rdquo; column, which will navigate you to the &ldquo;Results&rdquo; screen displaying all the respective tests&nbsp; with &ldquo;Result&rdquo; and related fields for each test.</p></li><li><p>Now select the flag appearing before the Referral Reason field and then select the Referral reason &amp; Institute.</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"375\" ac:original-width=\"970\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"image-20200330-103948.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /></li><li><p>Capture the notes and upload the desired file using respective features, if required.</p></li><li><p>Click on the &ldquo;Save&rdquo; button to save the entered details.</p></li><li><p>Referred Out test(s) count can be seen in the Lab Dashboard under Samples Collected - Today / Backlog - <strong>Referred Out</strong> column.</p></li><li><p>Count shown in <strong>Total </strong>column is including the Referred Out tests count.</p></li></ol><h3>2. Enter results for referred out lab test(s)</h3><ol><li><p>After login into the Laboratory app, mouse over on the &ldquo;Result&rdquo; menu at the top of the screen and click on &ldquo;Referred Out&rdquo; option in the Result menu drop down, which will navigate you to the &ldquo;Referrals&rdquo; screen.</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"308\" ac:original-width=\"1062\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Referred Out Tests.jpeg\" ri:version-at-save=\"2\" /></ac:image></li><li><p>In the &ldquo;Referrals&rdquo; screen, all the tests which have been referred out belonging to various patients will be displayed with Patient and Accession Number details.</p></li><li><p>Enter the results for desired tests in the corresponding &ldquo;Result&rdquo; field.</p></li><li><p>Click on the &ldquo;Notes&rdquo; icon and add the notes if required.</p></li><li><p>To upload a desired report file click on the corresponding &ldquo;Choose File&rdquo; button and select the desired file from your system&rsquo;s local disk.</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"633\" ac:original-width=\"1351\" ac:width=\"680\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Screenshot from 2021-03-04 20-46-50.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /></li><li><p>Check &ldquo;Mark as Done&rdquo; if the result entry is complete either by entering a result or by uploading a file on the same test or another test. Result for that test will go to validation phase if and only if the test is marked as done.</p></li><li><p>Click on the &ldquo;Save&rdquo; button to save the entered details.</p></li><li><p>Once the results have been entered and saved, the same will be available for validation along with the locally done tests in &ldquo;Validation&rdquo; screen.</p></li><li><p>Accordingly the &ldquo;Pending Validation&rdquo; column count in the Lab Dashboard will get updated.</p></li></ol><p /></ac:layout-cell><ac:layout-cell><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"toc\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"ee8c733f-d723-4bb6-9568-a049b4a0b444\" ac:macro-id=\"5d55e718-f27e-4b7b-951c-2c55e4c2d3d1\" /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"b872f364-a683-4fda-b01e-bfc3f6c7575f\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Feature Details</strong></p><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Laboratory Management\" ri:version-at-save=\"7\" /><ac:link-body>Feature Guide - Laboratory Management</ac:link-body></ac:link> </p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"5ba3348f-d274-4de0-a71d-9db4fe454215\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Implementation Details</strong></p><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Laboratory Module\" ri:version-at-save=\"22\" /><ac:link-body>Implementer's Guide - Laboratory Module</ac:link-body></ac:link> </p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></ac:layout-cell></ac:layout-section></ac:layout>",
